==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|inf=[[to]] [[blow]] [[the]] [[whistle]]|blows the whistle|blowing the whistle|blew the whistle}}

#{{idiom}} To [[disclose]] [[information]] to the [[public]] or to [[appropriate]] [[authority|authorities]] concerning the [[illegal]] or [[socially]] [[harmful]] actions of a person or group, especially a [[corporation]] or [[government]] [[agency]].
#:''Some laws say that people cannot be fired if she '''blows the whistle''' on an employer.''
#{{context|team sports}} To make a piercing sound which [[signal]]s a [[referee]]'s action or the end of a game.

====Synonyms====
*{{italbrac|disclose information}} [[tattle]], [[tell on]]

